    {
      "id": "claim_bda06701005646a89c43c2c868c2a2e3",
      "statement": "The prescribed stance toward a backtest is adversarial — treat it as a claim about the future stated in the language of the past, and assume it is overfit until it survives attempts to break it; the first question about a high Sharpe is how many strategies were tried before this one was kept, not how much money it would have made.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/backtest-interpretation.md#L11-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b45ec7db2979a1cbaa900a8fa0a4e196a1491180012cfe322cfc2401623d006:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95bb011ed2c14498bea8cb8ad14cb6b2",
      "statement": "The IS/OOS cliff is detected by the held-out final-30% Sharpe with the cliff check enforced against an in-sample Sharpe measured on the first 70% only, so the ratio cannot be gamed by blending the slices, and the gate renders the exact ratio in its detail string.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/backtest-interpretation.md#L35-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce0543783e68f23327f0fd4c7247fd40a89bfa3cd3523f6893cbc8cbff0f5812:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2104d9ea16ff47789fcd27e28e24387c",
      "statement": "Parameter sensitivity is caught at library level by PBO across C(16,8)=12,870 symmetric splits and at strategy level by DSR, which widens the Sharpe's standard error for non-normality and autocorrelation and deflates by expected best-of-N only where a candidate pool exists — on the curated library num_trials is 1, so neither deflation nor multiple-testing correction applies.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/backtest-interpretation.md#L56-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06ad504288cab7600e06a87432c37e4f0b1e9a3bc9828b5827029392d415e0da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_839823d1772e499b9b7973c0c245e2d2",
      "statement": "An unrealistically smooth equity curve is checked three ways: the look-ahead audit flags forward-data access, the analytics engine rejects close-on-close and close-on-open broker configurations that leak a bar's own close into its decision, and the closed-form expected one-year maximum drawdown flags a curve whose realised drawdowns are materially smaller than its own mu and sigma imply.",
      "evidence": [
